WEBVTT

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:18.460 line:86% position:50% align:center size:92%
Brothers and sisters, we have now arrived
in Bethsaida.

00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:22.520 line:86% position:50% align:center size:92%
Behind me you can see an introduction to
Bethsaida.

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:25.500 line:86% position:50% align:center size:92%
What happened here in Bethsaida?

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:29.340 line:86% position:50% align:center size:92%
On one occasion, the Lord Jesus came to
Bethsaida.

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:34.640 line:86% position:50% align:center size:92%
A blind man came before Him, crying out.

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:39.780 line:86% position:50% align:center size:92%
The disciples stopped him, but the Lord
Jesus said, Let him come to Me.

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:46.040 line:86% position:50% align:center size:92%
He asked, What do you want? The blind man
said, I want to see.

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:52.560 line:86% position:50% align:center size:92%
The Lord Jesus applied saliva to his
eyes.

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:57.000 line:86% position:50% align:center size:92%
He could see at once. The Lord Jesus
asked him what he saw.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.940 line:86% position:50% align:center size:92%
He said, People look like trees.

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:03.300 line:86% position:50% align:center size:92%
The Lord Jesus laid His hands on him
again.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:07.820 line:86% position:50% align:center size:92%
His eyes were restored, and he could see
clearly.

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:12.760 line:86% position:50% align:center size:92%
Brothers and sisters, this story took
place in Bethsaida.

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:19.040 line:86% position:50% align:center size:92%
For each of us, this means we need the
Lord to open our spiritual sight.

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:23.140 line:86% position:50% align:center size:92%
We were once blind and did not know our
Lord.

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:29.140 line:86% position:50% align:center size:92%
In daily life, we also often overlook
Him.

00:01:29.140 --> 00:01:34.740 line:86% position:50% align:center size:92%
We need to come to the Lord and ask Him
to open our sight.

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:37.720 line:86% position:50% align:center size:92%
How does the Lord open our sight? He uses
saliva.

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:41.320 line:86% position:50% align:center size:92%
What does the saliva signify? The words
that come from His mouth.

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:48.440 line:86% position:50% align:center size:92%
Brothers and sisters, we need His word to
open our eyes so that we can see.

00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:52.560 line:86% position:50% align:center size:92%
I see people; they look like trees
walking.

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:57.960 line:86% position:50% align:center size:92%
This illustrates our spiritual sight in
the early stages of spiritual recovery.

00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:03.140 line:86% position:50% align:center size:92%
What we see is like the blind man seeing
people as trees walking.

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:08.580 line:86% position:50% align:center size:92%
May the Lord lay His hands on us, so that
we may see everything clearly.
